---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Colophon"
  description="License, version, authorship, and contact for the HOOTL Safety Principles."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Colophon</h1>

      <h2>Authorship</h2>
      <p>
        Travis Winegar, with Claude (Anthropic) as collaborator across
        the drafting sessions of 2026.
      </p>

      <h2>Version</h2>
      <p>
        Principles of HOOTL Safety, v1.0 — published June 2026.
        Versioned at the document level; the eight principle numbers
        are stable across versions to preserve citation.
      </p>

      <h2>License</h2>
      <p>
        The spec text and prose documents are licensed under
        <a
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0)</a>.
        Cite the principles in your work — no permission required.
      </p>
      <p>
        Site source (Astro templates, CSS, configuration) is MIT
        licensed.
      </p>

      <h2>Cite</h2>
      <div class="cite-block">
        Winegar, T. (2026). <em>Principles of HOOTL Safety</em>
        (v1.0). Eight substrate-property principles for safe
        autonomous-agent operation. hootl.org.
      </div>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Comments, critiques, sector-specific extensions, and
        illustrative scenarios welcome via
        <a
          href="https://github.com/traviswinegar/hootl"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >GitHub issues</a>
        or
        <a href="mailto:travis@momusdev.com">travis@momusdev.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://agenticmd.org"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >agenticmd.org</a> — markup discipline for agent-consumed
          documentation
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AgentDNA</strong> — substrate-first agent operating
          framework; reference implementation in an agentic IDE
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Built with</h2>
      <p>
        Astro 4 · static-hosted · designed to render fast and survive
        link rot. The substrate is the truth; the site is the
        working surface.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
